<h1>Tools</h1>

<p>
  This page is dedicated to various tools this website uses, presenting them in isolation for ease of use. Other websites with useful components will also be linked.
</p>

<% mandarin_opts = ([:original] + Phoneticization::Converters::MANDARIN_SCHEMES.keys).map { |k| [k.to_s.tr("_"," "), k] } %>
<% cantonese_opts = ([:original] + Phoneticization::Converters::CANTONESE_SCHEMES.keys).map { |k| [k.to_s.tr("_"," "), k] } %>

<h2>Mandarin phoneticisation</h2>
<p>Mandarin has among the most amount of phoneticisations, which can be a bit overwhelming for some. This uses dohliam's <%= link_to "pinyin-rb", "https://github.com/dohliam/pinyin-rb" %> to display 13 of them.</p>

<%= form_with url: tools_phonetic_mandarin_path, method: :post, data: { turbo_frame: "mandarin_out" } do %>
  <label>From: <%= select_tag :from, options_for_select(mandarin_opts, :pinyin_numbers) %></label>
  <label style="margin-left:1em;">To: <%= select_tag :to, options_for_select(mandarin_opts, :pinyin_diacritics) %></label>
  <textarea name="input" rows="4" style="width:100%;" placeholder="han4 yu3 ..."></textarea>
  <button type="submit">Convert</button>
<% end %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "mandarin_out" do %><pre class="tool-output"></pre><% end %>

<h2>Cantonese phoneticisation</h2>
<%= form_with url: tools_phonetic_cantonese_path, method: :post, data: { turbo_frame: "cantonese_out" } do %>
  <label>From: <%= select_tag :from, options_for_select(cantonese_opts, :jyutping) %></label>
  <label style="margin-left:1em;">To: <%= select_tag :to, options_for_select(cantonese_opts, :ipa) %></label>
  <textarea name="input" rows="4" style="width:100%;" placeholder="gwong2 dung1 waa2 ..."></textarea>
  <button type="submit">Convert</button>
<% end %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag "cantonese_out" do %><pre class="tool-output"></pre><% end %>

<h2>Character data extractor</h2>

<p>This keeps the old Cangjie lookup behaviour, but also lets you pull other stored character data in bulk. Paste one character, a codepoint like U+8BF4, or a whole sentence to extract one row per unique Han character.</p>

<p>You can use this for flashcard enrichment: definitions, Kangxi entries, and readings can be previewed in-page or downloaded as CSV.</p>

<%= form_with url: tools_cangjie_path, method: :post, data: { turbo_frame: "cangjie_out" } do %>
  <p>
    <label>Extract:
      <%= select_tag :extract, options_for_select(extractor_options, "cangjie") %>
    </label>
  </p>

  <textarea name="input" rows="3" style="width: 100%;" placeholder="Character (e.g. 說) or U+8BF4 or Cangjie letters (e.g. ABC)
Or paste a sentence to get every unique character."></textarea>

  <p>
    <label><input type="checkbox" name="hkcards" value="1"> show HKCards table for Cangjie</label>
  </p>

  <p>
    <button type="submit">Extract</button>
    <button type="submit" name="download" value="csv" formtarget="_top" data-turbo="false">Download CSV</button>
  </p>
<% end %>

<%= turbo_frame_tag "cangjie_out" do %>
  <pre class="tool-output"></pre>
<% end %>

<h2>Lunar calendar date converter</h2>

<p>The Chinese lunar calendar uses the GanZhi system for formatting dates. This uses <%= link_to "a gem by elct9620", "https://github.com/elct9620/lunar_calendar" %> to easily convert between the Gregorian and Chinese dating systems. </p>

<%= form_with url: tools_lunar_path, method: :post, data: { turbo_frame: "lunar_out" } do %>
  <p>
    <label>Date picker:
      <input type="date" name="date_iso">
    </label>
  </p>

  <p>
    <label>Or paste a date:
      <input name="input" style="width: 100%;" placeholder="Examples: 2026-01-07 | 07/01/2026 | 7 Jan 2026 | today">
    </label>
  </p>

  <p><button type="submit">Convert</button></p>
<% end %>

<%= turbo_frame_tag "lunar_out" do %>
  <pre class="tool-output"></pre>
<% end %>

<h2>Numeral converter</h2>

<p>A simple mapper for Chinese numerals, accounting for some of the outliers and variant forms that occasionally pop up. It isn't perfect but will work for most things. I used this to produce a more robust Lunar calendar representation that you see on the site header!</p>

<%= form_with url: tools_numerals_path, method: :post, data: { turbo_frame: "numerals_out" } do %>
  <textarea name="input" rows="4" style="width: 100%;" placeholder="Paste text with numbers…"></textarea>

  <label><input type="checkbox" name="use_you" value="1"> use 有 for gaps</label>
  <label style="margin-left: 1em;"><input type="checkbox" name="use_abbrev" value="1"> use 廿/卅/卌</label>

  <div style="margin-top: 0.5em;">
    <button type="submit">Convert</button>
  </div>
<% end %>

<%= turbo_frame_tag "numerals_out" do %>
  <pre class="tool-output"></pre>
<% end %>
